Cart's pod uptime is continuous and there are no restarts, so the cause is not a pod lifecycle event. The evidence points to cart's calls into valkey-cart (`HGET`) becoming slow, and that slowness propagates upward. I checked my reasoning and have enough to answer.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "cart",
      "fault_kind": "database_call_slow",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT 'ab' p, service_name, span_name, COUNT(*) n, ROUND(AVG(duration)/1e6,1) avg_ms, ROUND(MAX(duration)/1e6,1) max_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='cart' AND span_name='HGET' GROUP BY 1,2,3 UNION ALL SELECT 'norm', service_name, span_name, COUNT(*), ROUND(AVG(duration)/1e6,1), ROUND(MAX(duration)/1e6,1) FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='cart' AND span_name='HGET' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "Cart's HGET calls to valkey-cart average 5.7 s in abnormal (max 6.0 s) versus 0.2 ms in normal."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_span_kind, COUNT(*) n, SUM(CASE WHEN attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) errs, ROUND(AVG(duration)/1e6,1) avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='cart' AND attr_span_kind='Server' GROUP BY 1,2 ORDER BY n DESC", "claim": "Cart server spans (AddItem, GetCart) take 60-70 s on average with errors; cart's own flagd and POST work stays sub-millisecond."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT service_name, metric, ROUND(AVG(value),1) avg_v FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE service_name IN ('cart','valkey-cart') AND metric IN ('k8s.pod.uptime','k8s.pod.cpu.usage') GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Cart and valkey-cart pods show continuous uptime and near-zero CPU, with no restarts, so the slowness is not a pod or CPU failure."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "cart", "to": "checkout", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, COUNT(*) n, SUM(CASE WHEN attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) errs, ROUND(AVG(duration)/1e6,1) avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE (service_name='checkout' AND span_name LIKE '%CartService/GetCart%') OR (service_name='checkout' AND span_name='oteldemo.CheckoutService/PlaceOrder') GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "Checkout's GetCart client calls to cart average about 85 s, and all 7 PlaceOrder server spans error."}]},
    {"from": "cart", "to": "frontend", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, COUNT(*) n, SUM(CASE WHEN attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) errs, ROUND(AVG(duration)/1e6,1) avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name IN ('grpc.oteldemo.CartService/AddItem','grpc.oteldemo.CartService/GetCart','POST /api/cart','GET /api/cart') GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "Frontend calls to CartService take 50-70 s on average, and the /api/cart requests return 500 errors."}]},
    {"from": "checkout", "to": "frontend", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_http_response_status_code, COUNT(*) n, ROUND(AVG(duration)/1e6,1) avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name IN ('grpc.oteldemo.CheckoutService/PlaceOrder','POST /api/checkout') GROUP BY 1,2,3,4", "claim": "Frontend's PlaceOrder client calls to checkout all error, averaging about 85 s, and POST /api/checkout returns 500."}]},
    {"from": "frontend", "to": "frontend-proxy", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_http_response_status_code, COUNT(*) n, ROUND(AVG(duration)/1e6,1) avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend-proxy' AND attr_span_kind='Server' GROUP BY 1,2,3,4", "claim": "Frontend-proxy ingress returns 504 and 500 errors with multi-second averages, and it carries the user-facing failures."}]}
  ]
}
```

